---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE, authors } from "../lib/blog-data.js";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About - ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`About ${SITE.name}: an independent magazine on writing, design, and the slow web.`}
  canonical="/about"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", to: "/" }, { label: "About" }]} />

    <header class="mt-6">
      <div class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">About</div>
      <h1 class="mt-2 font-serif text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.05]">
        A little corner for books, thoughts, and conversations.
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-article mt-10">
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is my little space on the internet where I talk about the books I’m reading, the ones I’ve loved, the ones that surprised me, and the ones I’m still trying to figure out how I feel about.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m Caroline, and I’ve always loved getting lost in a good book. My reading pile is usually a mix of thrillers, mysteries, historical fiction, literary fiction and translated books. I also have a particular weakness for short books that manage to leave a big impression.
      </p>
      <h2 id=""why-i-started"">Why I started Chapter Chats</h2>
      <p>
        I started Chapter Chats with Caroline because I wanted somewhere to share my thoughts about the books I read and have the kind of conversations that usually happen after finishing a really good book. Sometimes it’s about a character I loved, an ending I didn’t see coming, or a book that stayed in my head long after I turned the last page.
      </p>
      <h2 id="my-review-style">My Review Style</h2>
      <p>I don’t expect every book to be a five star read. Sometimes I love the story but not the ending. Sometimes the characters are what make a book memorable. Sometimes a beautifully written book simply isn’t for me. And sometimes I finish a book and immediately want to talk about it.
     </p>
    <p>That’s really what Chapter Chats with Caroline is about.</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 my-4 space-y-2">
  <li>Talking about books.</li>
  <li>Finding books worth picking up.</li>
  <li>Sharing the ones that surprised me.</li>
  <li>And hopefully discovering a few new favourites along the way.</li>
</ul>
<p class="mt-4 font-medium">
  So if you love talking about books as much as you love reading them, pull up a chair and let’s chat. ☕📖
</p>
      
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">Contributors</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          authors.map((author) => (
            <a href={`/authors/${author.slug}`} class="group flex items-start gap-3">
              <img src={author.avatar} alt="" width="48" height="48" class="h-12 w-12 rounded-full" />
              <div>
                <div class="font-serif text-base font-semibold group-hover:text-primary">{author.name}</div>
                <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">{author.bio}</div>
              </div>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
